  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers port established sequencing and CRISPR screen analyses to faster, reproducible open tools.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is re-engineering established analysis steps for speed, automation, and usability rather than introducing new statistical methods. deepTools4 rewrites core functions of its genomic sequencing suite, with benchmarked speed-ups and updated visualization. MAUDE-Py reimplements the MAUDE probabilistic framework in Python for sorting-based pooled CRISPR screens, adding automated baselines and null sampling. CLIPittyClip packages CLIP sequencing analysis as a local single-command pipeline from raw FASTQ to peak matrices and crosslink sites, with a 27-fold faster Python crosslink step (CLink). RSMViewer, a PyMOL plugin, addresses a downstream step by enabling batch visualization and superimposition of RNA structural motif instances. The items differ in domain, and RSMViewer is primarily a visualization tool rather than a reimplemented analysis pipeline.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-15"
}
